    "result_text": "The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS). The project's surefire config runs the acceptance test as its suite, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe create audit line already logged `id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and `membershipLevel`. I added `membershipNumber` to it in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java:710`:\n\n```java\nAUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={} membershipNumber={}\",\n    owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),\n    ownerMapper.membershipLevel(owner), ownerMapper.membershipNumber(owner));\n```\n\nThe pre-existing fields remain, and `membershipNumber` is derived via the same `ownerMapper.membershipNumber(owner)` used to populate the DTO \u2014 so the audit value matches what the API returns. The new `AcceptanceTest.coreAuditIncludesLevelAndNumber` and the full suite pass (BUILD SUCCESS).",
